{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Braided.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Category.Basic"],"declarations":25,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate.antipode_frobeniusForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate.antipode_frobeniusForm","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/frobenius-hopf-substrate.lean#L107-L107","doc":"**Antipode axiom 6 — `S` preserves the Frobenius form.**\n`S ≫ λ = λ`, so the pairing `⟨a, b⟩ = λ(ab)` is `S`-invariant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate.antipode_involutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate.antipode_involutive","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/frobenius-hopf-substrate.lean#L104-L104","doc":"**Antipode axiom 5 — `S` is involutive.**  `S ≫ S = 𝟙_A`.\n\nOn its own this pins nothing: `S = 𝟙_A` satisfies it on every group\ntested (`computations/probes/frobenius_hopf_intermediate_axioms_probe.py`).\nIt earns its place only alongside `antipode_anti_mul`, which `𝟙_A`\nfails whenever `A` is non-commutative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate.antipode_counit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate.antipode_counit","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/frobenius-hopf-substrate.lean#L97-L97","doc":"**Antipode axiom 4 — `S` preserves the counit.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate.antipode_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate.antipode_unit","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/frobenius-hopf-substrate.lean#L95-L95","doc":"**Antipode axiom 3 — `S` fixes the unit.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate.antipode_anti_comul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate.antipode_anti_comul","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/frobenius-hopf-substrate.lean#L92-L92","doc":"**Antipode axiom 2 — `S` reverses comultiplication.**\n`S ≫ Δ = Δ ≫ β ≫ (S ⊗ S)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate.antipode_anti_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate.antipode_anti_mul","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/frobenius-hopf-substrate.lean#L88-L88","doc":"**Antipode axiom 1 — `S` reverses multiplication.**\n`μ ≫ S = (S ⊗ S) ≫ β ≫ μ`, in elements `S(ab) = S(b)S(a)`.\n\nThe braiding is why this structure requires `[BraidedCategory C]`.  That\nis no new demand: the narrative already places the substrate at the level\nof a *quantum universe*, which is braided monoidal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate.comul_assoc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate.comul_assoc","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/frobenius-hopf-substrate.lean#L80-L80","doc":"Coassociativity — the \"coassociative\" of axiom 2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate.comul_counit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate.comul_counit","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/frobenius-hopf-substrate.lean#L78-L78","doc":"The right counit law is the mirror condition on the other tensor\nfactor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate.counit_comul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate.counit_comul","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/frobenius-hopf-substrate.lean#L75-L75","doc":"Left counit law — the \"counital\" of axiom 2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate.mul_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate.mul_one","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/frobenius-hopf-substrate.lean#L73-L73","doc":"The right unit law is the mirror condition on the other tensor factor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate.one_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate.one_mul","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/frobenius-hopf-substrate.lean#L71-L71","doc":"Left unit law — the \"unital\" of axiom 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate.snake_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate.snake_right","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/frobenius-hopf-substrate.lean#L66-L66","doc":"Snake identity (right): mirror non-degeneracy condition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate.snake_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate.snake_left","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/frobenius-hopf-substrate.lean#L61-L61","doc":"Snake identity (left): non-degeneracy of the Frobenius pairing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate.frobenius_relation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate.frobenius_relation","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/frobenius-hopf-substrate.lean#L57-L57","doc":"Frobenius relation: `Δ ∘ μ = (μ ⊗ id) ∘ α⁻¹ ∘ (id ⊗ Δ)` as a\nmorphism `A ⊗ A → A ⊗ A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate.mul_assoc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate.mul_assoc","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/frobenius-hopf-substrate.lean#L51-L51","doc":"Associativity of multiplication. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate.coevaluation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate.coevaluation","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/frobenius-hopf-substrate.lean#L49-L49","doc":"Coevaluation `η̃ : 𝟙 → A ⊗ A` dual to the Frobenius pairing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate.frobeniusForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate.frobeniusForm","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/frobenius-hopf-substrate.lean#L47-L47","doc":"Frobenius form `λ : A → 𝟙`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate.antipode","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate.antipode","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/frobenius-hopf-substrate.lean#L45-L45","doc":"Antipode `S : A → A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate.counit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate.counit","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/frobenius-hopf-substrate.lean#L43-L43","doc":"Counit `ε : A → 𝟙`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate.comul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate.comul","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/frobenius-hopf-substrate.lean#L41-L41","doc":"Comultiplication `Δ : A → A ⊗ A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate.unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate.unit","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/frobenius-hopf-substrate.lean#L39-L39","doc":"Unit `η : 𝟙 → A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate.mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate.mul","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/frobenius-hopf-substrate.lean#L37-L37","doc":"Multiplication `μ : A ⊗ A → A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate.obj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate.obj","kind":"def","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/frobenius-hopf-substrate.lean#L35-L35","doc":"The underlying object `A` in `C`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate.mk","kind":"ctor","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/frobenius-hopf-substrate.lean#L32-L32","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.FrobeniusHopfSubstrate","kind":"structure","line":23,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/frobenius-hopf-substrate.lean#L23-L107","doc":"**Frobenius–Hopf substrate**: a self-dual Frobenius–Hopf algebra\nobject `A` in a rigid monoidal category `C`.\n\nThe substrate carries multiplication, comultiplication, antipode,\nFrobenius form, and a self-duality isomorphism `A ≅ A∨` induced\nby the non-degenerate Frobenius pairing.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:frobenius-hopf-substrate}`\nRef: [kock2004] https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511615443 ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:frobenius-hopf-substrate","label":"def:frobenius-hopf-substrate","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/frobenius-hopf-substrate.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}